  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Casey Mize shut down Cleveland over six scoreless innings and the offense finally made that mean something.",
    "what_this_means": "The game was decided the moment it started. Never trailed, built a two-run lead in the second, and held it. That is not drama. That is control. Mize gave them air and the lineup breathed it in, scratching out five runs on ten hits without needing any one player to carry the weight. Rengifo hit a home run. Tatis got his two hits. That was enough. The bullpen closed the door. Estrada, Morejon, and Matsui combined for three scoreless frames with two strikeouts. This is what balanced looks like. The pitching held. The offense answered. Nothing wasted, nothing left stranded that mattered.",
    "what_to_watch": "Nolan McLean takes the mound for the Mets tonight with a 3.42 ERA. Walker Buehler counters with a 3.28 mark over his last four starts. The staff is beginning to settle, and if the bats stay honest, that becomes a real advantage.",
